tags: template

A setting of a network: some values of the domain are templates that the node fills at
each start from the environment variables of the start.

The value is the keys of the domain that are templates, sorted by their bytes and
separated by commas. Example: pow.block_id. The domain must have a value of key=value
lines. The value of each key in the list is exactly ${NAME}, where NAME matches
[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*. At a start, the node puts the value of the variable NAME of
Configuration.environment_variables in its place. The value of a variable must be UTF-8
with no newline. If a variable is absent, the node does not resolve the network at the
start, and the network is not in the configuration file. The service can resolve it
later with ResolveNetwork.

With no setting, the value of the domain is fixed: the node changes nothing. The node
is bound.

=== formal
class=setting
default=absent: the value of the domain is fixed
fill=at each start the node puts the UTF-8 value of the variable NAME of Configuration.environment_variables in its place; a value with a newline is not valid
missing=if a variable is absent, the node does not resolve the network at the start
name=template
place=service.network
template=the value of each such key is exactly ${NAME}, NAME matches [A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*
value=the keys of the value of the domain that are templates, sorted, separated by commas
